WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.445 --> 00:00:01.278
- Oh yeah.

00:00:02.463 --> 00:00:04.824
I've been making this
drink sound so attractive

00:00:04.824 --> 00:00:06.835
and desirable for all these years.

00:00:06.835 --> 00:00:08.763
Do you recognize me?

00:00:08.763 --> 00:00:11.263
I'm the Kool-Aid man, oh yeah.

00:00:13.778 --> 00:00:15.147
So I've had several people say,

00:00:15.147 --> 00:00:17.245
"It's hard to picture that that voice

00:00:17.245 --> 00:00:20.646
is actually coming from
you the human being."

00:00:20.646 --> 00:00:21.479
Oh yeah.

00:00:22.911 --> 00:00:25.323
They like the voice because
they don't know who I am.

00:00:25.323 --> 00:00:26.874
(upbeat music)

00:00:26.874 --> 00:00:28.775
When I first auditioned,
I think they wanted to get

00:00:28.775 --> 00:00:31.873
the flavor of the Kool-Aid man
that was already on the air.

00:00:31.873 --> 00:00:32.956
Oh yeah.

00:00:32.956 --> 00:00:35.513
When I came in, instead
of making it oh, oh,

00:00:35.513 --> 00:00:38.180
I wanted to go down, oh, oh, oh.

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:42.265
So he's gotta have a big deep voice.

00:00:42.265 --> 00:00:44.588
So I just thought start, like,
this guy wants to be an

00:00:44.588 --> 00:00:48.255
oh yeah, cool, and I
tried to make that voice

00:00:50.426 --> 00:00:53.275
you know, just kind of roll
around gutturally in my throat.

00:00:53.275 --> 00:00:54.934
Oh yeah.

00:00:54.934 --> 00:00:56.616
I can remember those sessions.

00:00:56.616 --> 00:00:58.268
After three hours of them just saying,

00:00:58.268 --> 00:01:00.253
"Okay, do it again, do
it again, do it again.

00:01:00.253 --> 00:01:01.634
"Try it again, how about lower?

00:01:01.634 --> 00:01:03.813
"More energy, more this, more Barry White.

00:01:03.813 --> 00:01:06.252
"Bigger, bigger, bigger, louder, louder."

00:01:06.252 --> 00:01:08.240
I'd be saying like, "What am I not doing,

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:09.301
that you're not getting?"

00:01:09.301 --> 00:01:10.207
But you're telling me to use a lot

00:01:10.207 --> 00:01:12.027
of high energy like David Lee Roth.

00:01:12.027 --> 00:01:13.381
I said, "The two don't mix."

00:01:13.381 --> 00:01:15.817
David Lee Roth's going, "Oh yeah,"

00:01:15.817 --> 00:01:18.883
doesn't mix with Barry
White going, "Oh yeah."

00:01:18.883 --> 00:01:20.472
So you have to find a happy balance.

00:01:20.472 --> 00:01:21.305
Oh yeah.

00:01:22.455 --> 00:01:23.455
Bottom's up.

